    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0364" n="274" xml:id="pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2246½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-09T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1918, 7
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 11, 11.30 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul at Harbin requests immediate repetition of following telegram received
                    to-day: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>July 8, 11 a.m. Inform Secretary of State immediately Horvat party left for Nikolsk
                            yesterday accompanied by Alexander, military
                            attaché, and many Japanese officers. Warner to join
                            Germans [Horvat’s] train <hi
                                rendition="#italic">en route</hi> and remain with them. Apparently
                            [Russians] in China prepared to support Horvat strongly but local Japanese authorities
                            disapprove, fearing failure which may involve railway. Local Chinese
                            governor will see me to-day to discuss feasibility of stopping all
                            political activities Chinese Eastern Railway.</p></quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >MacMurray</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
